\ port/strings.4 - relf's CSTRLEN, COMPARE and SCAN for a forth-vm-evolution
\ design. relf has them from libc (strlen, memcmp, memchr). A design's own
\ SCAN is a C loop where it has the gene (X_SCAN, all but smallest) and stops
\ at exactly c, as relf's does, except for a blank, which any control
\ character also meets; so SCAN is the design's but for a blank, and
\ CSTRLEN is the design's SCAN for the NUL. COMPARE and STR-EQ? are Forth:
\ a cell at a time while the strings agree, then bytes. STR-EQ? is the
\ shell's STR= (COMPARE 0=), which after.4 has compiled as a call to it - an
\ equality, so two lengths that differ end it at once.

BASE @  DECIMAL
1 CELLS CONSTANT PORT-CELL                     \ a cell's bytes: a design may have four
: CSTRLEN ( c-addr --- u )  DUP [ -1 1 RSHIFT ] LITERAL 0 SCAN DROP SWAP - ;
: SCAN ( c-addr1 u1 c --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ the design's, defined: not this one
  DUP 32 = 0= IF SCAN EXIT THEN
  >R BEGIN DUP WHILE OVER C@ R@ <> WHILE 1- SWAP 1+ SWAP REPEAT THEN R> DROP ;
: COMPARE ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 u2 --- n )
  ROT 2DUP - >R MIN                               ( a1 a2 min )  ( R: u2-u1 )
  BEGIN DUP PORT-CELL < 0= WHILE
    >R OVER @ OVER @ = WHILE PORT-CELL + SWAP PORT-CELL + SWAP R> PORT-CELL -
  REPEAT R> THEN
  0 ?DO
    OVER C@ OVER C@ - ?DUP IF NIP NIP 0< IF -1 ELSE 1 THEN UNLOOP R> DROP EXIT THEN
    1+ SWAP 1+ SWAP
  LOOP 2DROP
  R> DUP 0> IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN  0< IF 1 ELSE 0 THEN ;
: STR-EQ? ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 u2 --- f )
  ROT OVER <> IF DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN           ( a1 a2 u )
  BEGIN DUP PORT-CELL < 0= WHILE
    >R OVER @ OVER @ <> IF R> DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
    PORT-CELL + SWAP PORT-CELL + SWAP R> PORT-CELL -
  REPEAT
  BEGIN DUP WHILE
    >R OVER C@ OVER C@ <> IF R> DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
    1+ SWAP 1+ SWAP R> 1-
  REPEAT DROP 2DROP -1 ;
BASE !
